\details{
This helper is deliberately opt-in and stops in non-interactive sessions.
It asks the user to choose the person, score, optional weight, and facet
columns, prints reproducible code for the selected roles, then fits the
documented \code{RSM}/\code{MML} starting route before calling
\code{\link[=mfrm_results]{mfrm_results()}}. Use explicit \code{\link[=fit_mfrm]{fit_mfrm()}} calls in scripts, Quarto
documents, batch workflows, and reproducible analyses.

Testlet and random-rater results are not supported by this viewer. Use
\code{mfrm_report(res, output = "html")} or \code{\link[=export_mfrm_results]{export_mfrm_results()}} for their
static results and model-specific figures.

The viewer assumes that fitting, diagnostics, and section selection have
already happened through \code{\link[=mfrm_results]{mfrm_results()}}. This keeps GUI exploration
separate from reproducible analysis setup: the Replay tab displays the
\code{mfrm_results()} replay script stored in the result object.

The app includes tabs for overview/triage, QC evidence, APA-style report
text when \code{include = "publication"} or \code{"apa"} was used, available bias
screens, pathway plotting, unexpected-response inspection, generic tables,
generic plot routes, and replay code. QC, Report, Bias, and Pathway/Misfit
tabs show local section-status tables so unavailable or not-requested
sections are visible where users look for them. Bias-interaction follow-up
still requires an explicit facet-pair decision outside the viewer.

\code{shiny} is an optional dependency. Install it before using this viewer:
\code{install.packages("shiny")}.
}
\section{Why this helper is opt-in}{

Interactive prompts are useful at the console but are unsafe defaults for
reproducible analysis, unattended workflows, and manuscripts. The
helper therefore prints replay code and leaves the scripted route explicit.
}

